## 💡 Example: Complete Email Flow

**Step 1: Admin creates contact via UI**

```
POST /api/admin/contacts/create
→ Backend calls POST /contacts (Resend)
→ Contact created in Resend
→ Stored in local database
```

**Step 2: Admin creates audience**

```
POST /api/admin/audiences/create
→ Backend calls POST /audiences (Resend)
→ Audience created in Resend
```

**Step 3: Admin adds contacts to audience**

```
POST /api/admin/audiences/{id}/add-contacts
→ Backend calls POST /audiences/{id}/contacts (Resend) in bulk
→ Contacts linked to audience
```

**Step 4: Admin creates broadcast campaign**

```
POST /api/admin/campaigns/create
→ Backend calls POST /broadcasts (Resend)
→ Draft broadcast stored in Resend
→ Campaign stored in local database
```

**Step 5: Admin sends campaign**

```
POST /api/admin/campaigns/{id}/send
→ Backend calls POST /broadcasts/{id}/send (Resend)
→ Emails sent to all audience members
→ Status updated to "sending"
```

**Step 6: Webhooks fire as emails are opened/clicked**

```
Resend sends webhook to your endpoint
→ POST /api/webhooks/resend
→ Verify signature
→ Extract event (opened, clicked, bounced, etc.)
→ Store in analytics database
→ Dashboard updates in real-time
```

**Step 7: Admin views analytics**

```
GET /api/admin/analytics/summary
→ Query local analytics database
→ Calculate rates (open_rate = opened/sent * 100)
→ Return to dashboard
→ Display in charts & tables
```

